repository-code: 'https://github.com/Asrilioss/ElectrophyAnalysis'
abstract: >-
  A suite of three command-line pipelines and a graphical application that
  automate the analysis of whole-cell current-clamp recordings: extraction of
  Petilla-compliant intrinsic properties from 500 ms repetitive-firing
  protocols, kinetic characterization of single action potentials, and
  detection and area-under-curve quantification of slow depolarizations against
  a drift-tracking local baseline. Protocol-aware, batch-capable, deterministic
  and fully logged, with figure-ready Excel exports.
keywords:
  - electrophysiology
  - patch-clamp
  - current-clamp
  - action potential
  - intrinsic properties
  - reproducibility
  - Python
license: MIT
